UID: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-LEGEND
TITLE: How to read the colours
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: legend
PLACE: card
STATEMENT: >>>
Colour is only ever a tag, and every tag is written out beside it. What a colour means is the same on every screen of this page ([LINK: NAR-CANON-COLOURS]); the words below are this system's own.

- WORKS: green: stands as written under the current direction: Note
- FALLS OUT: slate: dissolved; the direction replaces it with something already in the model: Dissolved by
- UNADDRESSED: amber: the direction is silent on it: Note
- OPEN: blue: an open decision owns it: Owned by
- GAP: red: needed, and nobody has written it: Note
- HERE: grey: the layer this page is about
<<<
